msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:452
msgid "7 View the structure of the action type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:454
msgid ""
"Before sending an action goal, you need to know the structure of the action "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:456
msgid ""
"From the ``ros2 action list -t`` output, the type of ``/turtle1/"
"rotate_absolute`` is ``turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute``. To see its "
"structure, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:459
msgid "$ ros2 interface show turtlesim_msgs/action/RotateAbsolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:463
msgid "The output should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:465
msgid ""
"# The desired heading in radians\n"
"float32 theta\n"
"---\n"
"# The angular displacement in radians to the starting position\n"
"float32 delta\n"
"---\n"
"# The remaining rotation in radians\n"
"float32 remaining"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:476
msgid ""
"The section before the first ``---`` is the structure of the goal request. "
"The next section is the structure of the result. The last section is the "
"structure of the feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:481
msgid "8 Send an action goal from the command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:483
msgid "To send an action goal from the command line, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:485
msgid "$ ros2 action send_goal <action_name> <action_type> <values>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:489
msgid "``<values>`` need to be in YAML format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:491
msgid ""
"The goal field ``theta`` is the desired orientation in radians. The value is "
"absolute, not a relative turn amount. A value of ``1.57`` is about :math:"
"`\\pi/2` radians, so the turtle turns to face roughly a quarter turn from "
"the default rightward orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:495
msgid "Keep an eye on the Turtlesim window, then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:497
msgid ""
"$ ros2 action send_goal /turtle1/rotate_absolute turtlesim_msgs/action/"
"RotateAbsolute \"{theta: 1.57}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:503
msgid ""
"Waiting for an action server to become available...\n"
"Sending goal:\n"
"   theta: 1.57\n"
"\n"
"Goal accepted with ID: f8db8f44410849eaa93d3feb747dd444\n"
"\n"
"Result:\n"
"  delta: -1.568000316619873\n"
"\n"
"Goal finished with status: SUCCEEDED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:517
msgid "You should see the turtle rotating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:519
msgid ""
"All goals have a unique ID, shown in the return message. You can also see "
"the result, a field with the name ``delta``, which is the displacement to "
"the starting position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:522
msgid ""
"To see the feedback of this goal, add ``--feedback`` to the ``ros2 action "
"send_goal`` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:524
msgid ""
"$ ros2 action send_goal /turtle1/rotate_absolute turtlesim_msgs/action/"
"RotateAbsolute \"{theta: -1.57}\" --feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:530
msgid ""
"Sending goal:\n"
"   theta: -1.57\n"
"\n"
"Goal accepted with ID: e6092c831f994afda92f0086f220da27\n"
"\n"
"Feedback:\n"
"  remaining: -3.1268222332000732\n"
"\n"
"Feedback:\n"
"  remaining: -3.1108222007751465\n"
"\n"
"…\n"
"\n"
"Result:\n"
"  delta: 3.1200008392333984\n"
"\n"
"Goal finished with status: SUCCEEDED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:550
msgid ""
"You should continue to receive feedback, the remaining radians, until the "
"goal is complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:555
msgid "9 View the communication between an action client and action server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:559
msgid "This feature is available on ``Kilted Kaiju`` or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:561
msgid ""
"To see the data communication between an action client and an action server, "
"use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:563
msgid "$ ros2 action echo <action_name> <optional arguments/action_type>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:567
msgid ""
"``ros2 action echo`` requires action introspection, which is disabled by "
"default. To enable it, call ``configure_introspection`` after creating an "
"action client or server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:570
msgid ""
"Start up the ``fibonacci_action_server`` and ``fibonacci_action_client``, "
"enabling the ``action_server_configure_introspection`` parameter for "
"demonstration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:572
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run action_tutorials_cpp fibonacci_action_server --ros-args -p "
"action_server_configure_introspection:=contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:576
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run action_tutorials_py fibonacci_action_client --ros-args -p "
"action_client_configure_introspection:=contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:580
msgid ""
"To see the action communication between ``fibonacci_action_server`` and "
"``fibonacci_action_client``, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions.rst:582
